{"seconds": 41.2, "exit": 0, "final": "Great! Same pattern \u2014 Rd7+ forks the king and bishop. The key idea is that **Rxa7+** wins material by force through a rook fork.\n\n**Best move:** Rxa7+\n\n**Main line:** Rxa7+ Kd8 Rd7+ Ke8 Rxg7 (winning the bishop)\n\n**Motif:** fork\n\n**Explanation for a club player:**\n\nWhen your opponent's king moves to safety from a check, look for a follow-up check that attacks another piece simultaneously. Here, after Rxa7+ Kd8, the rook can give check on d7 while forking the undefended bishop on g7. Black must move the king again, and White simply captures the bishop, winning a whole piece. The lesson: **always scan for a second check that combines with an attack on an undefended piece.**\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rxa7+\", \"line\": [\"Rxa7+\", \"Kd8\", \"Rd7+\", \"Ke8\", \"Rxg7\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5fb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5fb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "5fb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/p1k3bp/1p6/6p1/R1PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K w - - 1 27", "move": "Rxa7+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/R1k3bp/1p6/6p1/2PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K b - - 0 27", "move": "Kd8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rb1/R1k3bp/1p6/6p1/2PN4/1P1Pp2P/1P4P1/7K b - - 0 27", "move": "Kb8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "